rs480: add the 189 fieldless 0x4xxx UNDOC registers to the force-clock probe table

Census 2026-06-14 (rs482_undoc_4xxx_3d_pipe_register_census.tsv) found 189
fieldless 0x4xxx UNDOC 3D-pipe registers that the mesa r300 driver never emits,
so their function cannot be recovered from driver usage.  This appends them to
rs480_force_clock_3d_list (indices 42..230) so the force-clock-then-read node can
sample them under the forced 3D clock.

The node mechanism is unchanged; it forces the whole 3D clock set before each
read.  The rows are appended after the 0035 control entries; existing indices
0..41 stay stable.  Ordered GA/GB/SU first (the most force-clock-proven domain),
then SC/RS, RB3D/ZB/FG, US/TX, and PIPE3D last (least characterized).  These are
UNKNOWN offsets: the attended sweep reads them one at a time, boot_id-guarded,
and a stall needs a cold power cycle (this reset-less K8 has no usable hardware
watchdog -- the SB600 TCO control write itself wedges the host).  Disarmed by
default.

Assisted-by: Claude (Opus 4.8)
---
